cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use East Room, please cite it as below.
title: "East Room: read whole books in the author's own words, paced for a restless mind"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jawad
    given-names: Intesar
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/intesarjawad/eastroom"
abstract: >-
  East Room takes a book file (EPUB, PDF, comic archive or plain text) and walks the reader through
  every word of it: a highlighter moves at a chosen pace, the book is cut into short parts where
  its author cut it, and the place is kept across devices. It runs on the reader's own computer.
keywords:
  - reading
  - EPUB
  - ADHD
  - accessibility
  - local-first
